  "content": "Here is the step-by-step deterministic arithmetic solution for the given values.\n\n**Given Values:**\n*   $a = 137$\n*   $b = 29$\n*   $c = 11$\n\n**Expression to Compute:**\n$$ (a \\cdot b + c^3) - (a - b) \\cdot c $$\n\n### Step 1: Compute $a \\cdot b$\n$$ 137 \\cdot 29 $$\n\nTo perform this multiplication manually:\n$$ 137 \\cdot 29 = 137 \\cdot (30 - 1) $$\n$$ 137 \\cdot 30 = 4110 $$\n$$ 137 \\cdot 1 = 137 $$\n$$ 4110 - 137 = 3973 $$\n\nSo, **$a \\cdot b = 3973$**.\n\n### Step 2: Compute $c^3$\n$$ 11^3 = 11 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 11 $$\n$$ 11 \\cdot 11 = 121 $$\n$$ 121 \\cdot 11 = 1331 $$\n\nSo, **$c^3 = 1331$**.\n\n### Step 3: Compute the first parenthesis $(a \\cdot b + c^3)$\n$$ 3973 + 1331 $$\n\nCalculation:\n  $$ 3973 $$\n+ $$ 1331 $$\n-----------\n  $$ 5304 $$\n\nSo, the first term is **$5304$**.\n\n### Step 4: Compute $(a - b)$\n$$ 137 - 29 $$\n\nCalculation:\n$$ 137 - 29 = 108 $$\n\nSo, **$(a - b) = 108$**.\n\n### Step 5: Compute the second term $(a - b) \\cdot c$\n$$ 108 \\cdot 11 $$\n\nCalculation:\n$$ 108 \\cdot 11 = 108 \\cdot (10 + 1) $$\n$$ 108 \\cdot 10 = 1080 $$\n$$",
